Ladybird picks the font of each character of SVG text by the character’s
emoji presentation, keeps an emoji sequence in one font, and draws the
glyphs of a color font as they are, wherever the text has a fill or
a stroke. Blink does the same: FontFallbackIterator::Next() takes the
emoji presentation into account, HarfBuzzShaper shapes a sequence as
one cluster, and Skia draws a color glyph as an image for a fill pass
and for a stroke pass alike. WebKit picks the font in FontCascadeFonts::
glyphDataForCharacter(), and draws through SVGTextBoxPainter::
paintTextWithShadows(). Gecko picks the font in gfxFontGroup::
FindFontForChar(), but paints SVG text as glyph outlines whenever
SVGTextFrame::ShouldRenderAsPath() says so — with a stroke or a fill
opacity, e.g. — where a bitmap glyph draws nothing.

On macOS, with Apple Color Emoji: Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0,
and WebKit 26.5 all draw an emoji in its own colors whatever the fill
color is, and draw nothing for a fill of none or of transparent. Chrome
and WebKit draw the emoji for a stroke without a fill, and draw it
translucent for a fill-opacity, as Ladybird does; Firefox draws nothing
in either case. Chrome applies the alpha of a translucent fill color
to the emoji, as Ladybird does; WebKit doesn’t. And in all three, as in
Ladybird, three emoji that zero width joiners make one are as long as
one emoji, in text whose own font has a glyph for the joiner.

Where lengthAdjust is spacingAndGlyphs, Ladybird moves a color glyph
to where it lands, but doesn’t stretch it; Blink and WebKit stretch it.
And Ladybird leaves color glyphs out of a clipping path, where Blink and
WebKit clip to their silhouettes.

After a joiner, a character whose variation selector asks for its text
presentation gets its font by that presentation, rather than staying
in the emoji font: UTS #51 allows no text presentation sequence in an
emoji ZWJ sequence. That rule comes from the specification alone, since
the fonts at hand show no difference between the two in any engine. A
joiner that follows a character that’s no emoji joins nothing either:
The character after it gets its font from the cascade, as any other
character does. The lines the test has for that case print the same in
the three engines as in Ladybird.
